    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Bride Armour" hidden="false" id="cbac-842e-e206-5459" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Bride Armour" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="2ab4-71f1-772d-305a">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">*Elite Wych Cult ceremonial combat armour reserved for the most accomplished gladiatorial duelists and ceremonial blood brides of the arenas, built from refined flex-plating, nerve-linked reactive mesh and pain-synchronized reinforcement fibers.* A model equipped with bride armour gains a 5+ Invulnerable Save. In addition, this improves to a 4+ Invulnerable Save in the Fight phase.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <infoLinks>
        <infoLink name="Invulnerable Save (X)" id="6cb0-85bd-7ff0-120f" hidden="false" targetId="2d12-951d-7304-58f8" type="rule">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" field="name" value="Invulnerable Save (5+)" />
          </modifiers>
        </infoLink>
      </infoLinks>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Fleshcrafted Plates" hidden="false" id="7ed6-07a9-1a1c-50f3" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Fleshcrafted Plates" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="3bc6-08d4-9224-033a">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">*Dense, ossified bio-armour grafts grown through accelerated ossification cycles and reinforced with synthetic tendon lattices.* A model equipped with fleshcrafted plates gains a 6+ Armour Save, Feel No Pain (5+), and It Will Not Die (6+). In addition, models equipped with fleshcrafted plates do not suffer Instant Death. Instead, when affected by an attack or effect that would cause Instant Death, the model instead suffers D3 Wounds.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Ghostplate Armour" hidden="false" id="a9da-3776-40a0-9323" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Ghostplate Armour" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="b0a8-f24c-eb05-53f4">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">*Phase-laced composite armour that partially desynchronizes from realspace during impact events.* A model equipped with ghostplate armour gains a 4+ Armour Save and a 6+ Invulnerable Save. In addition, if the model already has an Invulnerable Save, it is improved by +1 to a maximum of 4+.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <infoLinks>
        <infoLink name="Invulnerable Save (X)" id="9fff-09f0-08e3-d454" hidden="false" targetId="2d12-951d-7304-58f8" type="rule">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" field="name" value="Invulnerable Save (6+)" />
          </modifiers>
        </infoLink>
      </infoLinks>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Haemonculus Armour" hidden="false" id="9988-785c-dd4a-756f" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Haemonculus Armour" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="84b2-ab15-7d43-81e5">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">A model equipped with Haemonculus armour gains a 4+ Armour Save and the Feel No Pain (5+) special rule. In addition, attacks with the Poisoned special rule targeting a model equipped with Haemonculus armour suffer -1 Strength (to a minimum of 1) as the armour's internal toxin filtration systems rapidly neutralize hostile biochemical agents. A model equipped with Haemonculus armour may ignore the first failed Dangerous Terrain test it suffers each turn.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Haemoxyte Armour" hidden="false" id="75bb-1ac1-37ca-776a" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Haemoxyte Armour" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="9fc4-727f-b504-1680">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">*Living bio-armour grown from harvested flesh matrices, semi-autonomous and continuously adaptive.* A model equipped with Haemoxyte armour gains a 5+ Armour Save and the Feel No Pain (5+) special rule.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Incubi Armour" hidden="false" id="3279-2291-3fa1-53b2" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Incubi Armour" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="c08d-bc3e-cb55-00bd">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">*A heavily reinforced shrine-warplate of layered psycho-reactive plating, hardened ablative mesh and localized shadowfield emitters, engineered for close-quarters execution warfare.* A model equipped with Incubi armour gains a 3+ Armour Save and a 5+ Invulnerable Save. This Invulnerable Save may not be improved beyond 4+ by any means unless explicitly stated otherwise. In addition, a model equipped with Incubi armour gains Battle-hardened (1) during any Fight phase in which it successfully Charged or was Charged.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <infoLinks>
        <infoLink name="Invulnerable Save (X)" id="3f33-f98f-171c-d85a" hidden="false" targetId="2d12-951d-7304-58f8" type="rule">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" field="name" value="Invulnerable Save (5+)" />
          </modifiers>
        </infoLink>
      </infoLinks>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Kabalite Armour" hidden="false" id="3dae-5443-5084-9de0" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Kabalite Armour" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="9c15-2fee-1267-bd91">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">*Segmented mesh plating, toxin-resistant underlayers and lightweight adaptive composites, made for mass deployment and extreme mobility.* A model equipped with Kabalite armour gains a 5+ Armour Save.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Mesh Armour" hidden="false" id="c40a-f65b-84b1-69c3" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Mesh Armour" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="7301-343a-c553-c7d2">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">A model with mesh armour has a 4+ Armour Save.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Shadow Armour" hidden="false" id="43e3-d8b8-cd41-fe5d" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Shadow Armour" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="1270-2014-0a26-fb68">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">A model with shadow armour has a 6+ Armour Save and a 5+ Invulnerable Save. In addition, units with this armour are treated as if they are 6" further away than they are and cannot be targeted outside of 12" when Night Fighting rules are being used. Equipment or rules that ignore Night Fighting also ignore this rule.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <infoLinks>
        <infoLink name="Invulnerable Save (X)" id="f6fc-9be0-b094-d36f" hidden="false" targetId="2d12-951d-7304-58f8" type="rule">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" field="name" value="Invulnerable Save (5+)" />
          </modifiers>
        </infoLink>
      </infoLinks>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Wrack Armour" hidden="false" id="4379-c6b1-57d3-af91" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Wrack Armour" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="d5e5-585c-0f62-00be">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">*Living bio-armour grown from harvested flesh matrices refined through Haemonculus conditioning processes.* A model equipped with Wrack armour gains a 6+ Armour Save and the Feel No Pain (6+) special rule.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Wych Armour" hidden="false" id="9a01-d1c3-5a97-430b" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Wych Armour" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="6121-7a08-de1d-ab96">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">*Gladiatorial combat armour of segmented flex-plating, impact-dampening bio-gel and motion-reactive fibers tuned for agility and dueling survival.* A model equipped with Wych armour gains a 6+ Invulnerable Save. In addition, this improves to a 5+ Invulnerable Save in the Fight phase.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <infoLinks>
        <infoLink name="Invulnerable Save (X)" id="5153-f3be-40ea-e5d8" hidden="false" targetId="2d12-951d-7304-58f8" type="rule">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" field="name" value="Invulnerable Save (6+)" />
          </modifiers>
        </infoLink>
      </infoLinks>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Bladevanes" hidden="false" id="53e6-bfba-0819-4e03" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Bladevanes" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="77d6-4d06-4868-f21f">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">*Mono-molecular gravitic cutting fins mounted along the hulls of Drukhari anti-grav craft and aerial assault platforms. Designed primarily for high-speed attack runs and terror strikes, bladevanes transform the movement of the vehicle itself into a weapon, slicing through infantry formations with impossible precision as the craft passes overhead.* A model equipped with bladevanes may inflict Hits against one enemy Infantry unit that it moved over during the Movement phase. That unit suffers D3 Strength 4 AP 4 Hits with Rending (6+). If the model has a Movement characteristic of 14 or greater, increase the number of Hits inflicted to D6 instead. These Hits are resolved as Shooting Attacks and may only be inflicted once per phase regardless of how many units the model moved over.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Chain-snares" hidden="false" id="dbd2-9152-eeac-f759" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Chain-snares" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="0d71-66ce-9157-74f5">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">*Weighted mono-filament drag chains and hooked gravitic tether systems mounted beneath Drukhari skimmers and assault craft. As the vehicle passes through enemy formations, the snares tear apart infantry, drag victims into the air and scatter formations into chaos.* A model equipped with chain-snares may inflict Hits against one enemy Infantry unit that it moved over during the Movement phase. That unit suffers D3 Strength 5 AP - Hits with Shred and Pinning. If the model has a Movement characteristic of 14 or greater, increase the number of Hits inflicted to D6 instead. In addition, enemy units that suffer one or more unsaved Wounds from chain-snares reduce their Movement characteristic by 2 until the end of their next Turn. These Hits are resolved as Shooting Attacks and may only be inflicted once per phase regardless of how many units the model moved over.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Clone Field" hidden="false" id="f4b4-c686-54a8-09d4" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Clone Field" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="6dbe-5062-dba1-8b7f">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">*An advanced holographic displacement system that generates combat-accurate positional duplicates of the bearer, each offset by microsecond temporal phase divergence.* Enemy models suffer -1 Weapon Skill when resolving Melee attacks against the bearer. In addition, the bearer cannot be affected by Precision Shots, Precision Strikes, or any effect that allows attacks to bypass normal targeting rules unless that rule explicitly ignores all forms of targeting protection.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Crucible of Malediction" hidden="false" id="a69a-f92f-6111-9299" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Crucible of Malediction" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="edd4-6220-2f03-735c">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">*A warp containment and psychic disruption relic of psycho-reactive alloys, daemon-etched insulation lattices and captured warp resonance cores.* All units within 12" of one or more models equipped with a Crucible of Malediction gain Adamantium Will (4+). Once per battle, during any Psychic phase, the bearer may activate the Crucible. When activated, all Psyker units within 12" must immediately take Psychic tests. Any unit that fails suffers Perils of the Warp and D3 Wounds that cannot be saved by Armour Saves or Invulnerable Saves. In addition, all Psyker units within range suffer -1 Leadership until the end of the turn.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Enhanced Aethersails" hidden="false" id="3059-caf0-e5b0-d59c" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Enhanced Aethersails" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="14c2-ec86-feb0-dc8f">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">*Propulsion augmentation that manipulates atmospheric density gradients, gravitational shear vectors and localized dimensional pressure to generate extreme acceleration and evasive manoeuvring.* A model equipped with enhanced aethersails increases its Movement characteristic by +4. After completing any movement, the model gains Shrouded (5+). This effect stacks with other sources of Shrouded but cannot improve beyond Shrouded (4+). Enhanced aethersails also allow unrestricted traversal over vertical terrain and battlefield elevation differences, treating such movement as part of standard movement resolution.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Flickerfield" hidden="false" id="ea67-2da1-460d-87a3" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Flickerfield" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="81b6-bac9-edd8-bba3">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">*An unstable phase-displacement shield that displaces incoming attacks across fractional temporal probability states.* A model equipped with a flickerfield gains a 6+ Invulnerable Save. If the model already has an Invulnerable Save, improve it by +1 to a maximum of 4+. This improvement applies before any other modifiers unless explicitly stated otherwise.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <infoLinks>
        <infoLink name="Invulnerable Save (X)" id="1410-5d23-1b20-c337" hidden="false" targetId="2d12-951d-7304-58f8" type="rule">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" field="name" value="Invulnerable Save (6+)" />
          </modifiers>
        </infoLink>
      </infoLinks>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Grav-talons" hidden="false" id="1a08-0814-5caa-79f0" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Grav-talons" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="f989-86b8-e223-5b4b">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">*Anti-gravity disruption systems that generate localized gravitational inversion fields at the point of impact, destabilizing an enemy's balance and combat timing.* Enemy units charged by one or more models equipped with grav-talons suffer -2 Initiative until the end of the Fight phase. In addition, if a model equipped with grav-talons arrives via Deep Strike and declares or completes a Charge in the same turn, the target unit must immediately take a Pinning test at -2 Leadership.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Grisly Trophies" hidden="false" id="df4d-c184-20a0-f107" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Grisly Trophies" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="2431-173e-7bd3-07f3">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">*Psycho-resonant terror amplifiers built from preserved victim remains, neural imprint residues and emotionally charged biological fragments.* Enemy Infantry and Cavalry units within 6" of one or more models equipped with grisly trophies suffer Fear (2). This effect is applied continuously while within range.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Haywire Grenades" hidden="false" id="c538-f2c2-2881-53d8" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Haywire Grenades" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="d7eb-d63a-87d4-74f4">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">*Electromagnetic disruption charges designed to overload mechanical systems, disrupt servo-motors and collapse armoured integrity through cascading energy feedback failure.* A model equipped with haywire grenades may throw them as a grenade, or use them as a Melee weapon with the haywire grenades – melee profile in the Armoury. These attacks are treated as system disruption events rather than conventional explosive damage.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <entryLinks>
        <entryLink import="true" name="Haywire grenades" hidden="false" id="f4f4-3959-02f5-9aaa" type="selectionEntry" targetId="bdfa-f987-49c9-aecc">
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="min" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="11d6-76f0-e32e-6073" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" />
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="dd70-8582-5390-ab25" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" />
          </constraints>
        </entryLink>
      </entryLinks>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Kabalite Icon" hidden="false" id="a152-81fc-5599-3dc5" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Kabalite Icon" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="1fba-8d3d-6bbb-d17a">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">A unit that includes one or more Kabalite icons gains +1 Leadership while at least one model equipped with a Kabalite icon remains alive. In addition, friendly Kabalite units within 6" of one or more models equipped with a Kabalite icon gain the Line Sub-type.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Mirage Veil" hidden="false" id="3b0c-6130-7bee-9a87" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Mirage Veil" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="df8a-a5f3-e615-8b07">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">*Layered false positional projections across visual, thermal and predictive targeting spectra.* A model equipped with a mirage veil cannot be affected by Precision Shots or Precision Strikes. In addition, it gains Shrouded (6+). This Shrouded effect stacks with other sources but cannot improve beyond Shrouded (4+).</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Nightmare Doll" hidden="false" id="56c1-a3ff-7d85-48ed" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Nightmare Doll" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="35e0-98b3-894e-945d">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">*A soul-binding containment construct that anchors its bearer's essence to reality through redundant psychic imprints.* The first time a model equipped with a nightmare doll would be removed as a casualty, it remains in play with 1 Wound remaining instead of being destroyed. In addition, the bearer gains Eternal Warrior and Fear (1), which may be increased up to Fear (3) through additional effects.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Night Shields" hidden="false" id="b98f-3f97-3baf-b4bd" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Night Shields" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="10b2-e238-21b4-be09">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">*Targeting degradation fields that manipulate ballistic computation, sensor resolution and range estimation.* Enemy units targeting a model equipped with night shields for ranged attacks treat that model as 6" further away than its actual position. In addition, any ranged attack made at over 18" is resolved as Snap Shots.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Pain Amplifier" hidden="false" id="ac75-85a3-f6b5-10cb" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Pain Amplifier" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="5b26-f4ce-e292-ceeb">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">*A psycho-resonant device that aligns battlefield suffering thresholds across several units, converting pain into combat efficiency.* A unit containing one or more models equipped with a pain amplifier may select two effects from the Power From Pain table each time it would normally select one. Both effects apply simultaneously unless explicitly restricted by other rules.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Phantasm Grenade Launcher" hidden="false" id="ad67-de96-ebec-89fd" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Phantasm Grenade Launcher" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="d86e-a259-1e74-d4c2">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">*A psycho-sonic launcher that emits hallucinogenic fragmentation waves designed to destabilize perception, memory and command coordination.* Enemy units that suffer one or more hits from this weapon suffer -2 Leadership until the end of the turn. In addition, any unit that fails a Pinning test caused by this weapon gains the Disordered condition until the end of the turn. Its profile is in the Armoury.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <entryLinks>
        <entryLink import="true" name="Phantasm grenade launcher" hidden="false" id="104b-d62c-d944-845b" type="selectionEntry" targetId="216f-8d5d-6f0d-47a8">
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="min" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="59c6-c41a-69d3-3950" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" />
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="1baf-1b21-74bc-4114" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" />
          </constraints>
        </entryLink>
      </entryLinks>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Plasma Grenades" hidden="false" id="005c-5bb5-0514-846c" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Plasma Grenades" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="7a3f-fd07-19c2-02e6">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">*Assault disruption devices that generate localized energy collapse fields to neutralize defensive positions before close engagement.* A unit equipped with plasma grenades gains Assault Grenades. In addition, enemy units gain no benefit from Cover Saves or Defensive Grenade rules against Charge Attacks made by this unit. They may also be thrown using the plasma grenades profile in the Armoury.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <entryLinks>
        <entryLink import="true" name="Plasma grenades" hidden="false" id="431a-63d3-516b-0138" type="selectionEntry" targetId="f73e-6418-eca1-dd80">
          <constraints>
            <constraint type="min" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="cf1f-b1dc-fb37-f51f" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" />
            <constraint type="max" value="1" field="selections" scope="parent" shared="true" id="6132-435b-2424-55d5" percentValue="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" />
          </constraints>
        </entryLink>
      </entryLinks>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Reaver Jetbike" hidden="false" id="b851-1fb4-f6f4-8f8f" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Reaver Jetbike" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="cb7c-af52-1f15-a8ad">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">*An anti-gravity cavalry platform built for extreme-velocity assault warfare, combining gravitic lift fields, inertial dampening matrices and blade vane propulsion.* A model equipped with a Reaver jetbike gains the Cavalry (Antigrav) unit type and has its Movement characteristic set to 16. The model treats all terrain as open ground for movement purposes, including vertical terrain, ruins and battlefield elevation changes, unless a rule explicitly prevents Antigrav traversal. The model gains Hammer of Wrath (1), Fleet (1), and Hit &amp; Run. Reaver jetbikes also interact with movement-based weapon systems such as chain-snares and stinger pods, enabling full resolution of overflight-triggered effects during any valid movement path. Reaver jetbikes are equipped with splinter rifles.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Scourge Wings" hidden="false" id="aa99-91e0-08a2-dc17" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Scourge Wings" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="c266-c493-0d12-3e18">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">*Bio-engineered skeletal and muscular modifications grafted directly into the body by ancient Drukhari fleshcraft: psycho-reactive wing structures of living musculature, gravitic membrane tissues and hyper-light skeletal reinforcement. The transformation is agonizing and irreversible.* A model equipped with Scourge wings gains the Jump Infantry unit type and adds +6" to its Movement. The model gains Deep Strike, Fleet (1), and Hit &amp; Run. During the Movement phase, a model equipped with Scourge wings may move over terrain and models freely, ignoring vertical movement restrictions as normal for Jump Infantry units. After firing weapons during the Shooting phase, a model equipped with Scourge wings may immediately make an additional 6" Jet Pack move. This movement follows all normal Jet Pack movement restrictions and may not be used to enter base contact with enemy models.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Shadowfield" hidden="false" id="c2f9-1b6f-b388-79dc" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Shadowfield" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="2aca-fe1c-b182-ff46">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">*An unstable personal defense matrix that displaces incoming attacks across micro-temporal probability fractures.* A model equipped with a shadowfield gains a 2+ Invulnerable Save. If a Saving Throw made using this Invulnerable Save is failed, the shadowfield immediately overloads and ceases functioning for the remainder of the battle.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <infoLinks>
        <infoLink name="Invulnerable Save (X)" id="e4f1-3e18-dd22-3d36" hidden="false" targetId="2d12-951d-7304-58f8" type="rule">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" field="name" value="Invulnerable Save (2+)" />
          </modifiers>
        </infoLink>
      </infoLinks>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Shadow Glide Harness" hidden="false" id="0b28-6888-cb0a-54f1" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Shadow Glide Harness" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="b62f-e122-073c-7cb7">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">*A stealth mobility system combining low-altitude gravitic glide, optical suppression fields and inertial decoupling arrays.* A model equipped with a shadow glide harness gains the Deep Strike special rule. In addition, if the model has not moved during its Movement phase, it gains Shrouded (6+). This stacks with other sources of Shrouded but cannot exceed Shrouded (4+).</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <infoLinks>
        <infoLink name="Deep Strike" id="32de-c00a-532f-8818" hidden="false" targetId="f1e1-986f-c783-ca9e" type="rule" />
      </infoLinks>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Shock Prow" hidden="false" id="a116-3477-d057-866e" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Shock Prow" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="0a03-9c6c-80a6-2121">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">*A kinetic impact reinforcement system that channels forward velocity through reinforced prow assemblies and gravitic compression vanes.* A model equipped with a shock prow gains Hammer of Wrath (2). If it already has Hammer of Wrath, increase its value by +2 to a maximum of 4. In addition, Charges made by this model gain Exoshock (5+) and Breaching (6+). Shock prows function primarily during Charge resolution but may also apply during any rule that generates collision-based movement impacts.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Skyboard" hidden="false" id="0ab1-028c-570d-8f15" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Skyboard" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="a214-86ad-7bf2-06a2">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">*An anti-gravity personal platform used by Hellion raiders for high-speed aerial assault and rapid insertion warfare.* A model equipped with a skyboard gains Cavalry (Antigrav) and has its Movement characteristic set to 14. The model treats all terrain as open ground, including vertical structures and battlefield debris fields. The model gains Hammer of Wrath (1), Fleet (1), and Hit &amp; Run. Skyboards are equipped with splinter pods, and fully interact with overflight-triggered systems such as stinger pods and chain-snares.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Slave Snares" hidden="false" id="2622-9761-e170-b110" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Slave Snares" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="6f6a-c6b1-3937-918c">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">*Tethering filaments, gravitic drag fields and neuro-inhibitory feedback loops designed to immobilize fleeing enemies.* Enemy units suffering casualties from a model equipped with slave snares reduce their Movement characteristic by 2. In addition, enemy units within 3" of such a model cannot make Reactions while Falling Back.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Soul-sight Helm" hidden="false" id="9e67-11bb-e2cb-0bf8" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Soul-sight Helm" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="6935-8dc0-094e-c1e7">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">*A predictive targeting system that isolates enemy command structures through neural mapping and threat hierarchy indexing.* A model equipped with a soul-sight helm gains Precision Shots (5+) and Ignore Cover. Once per battle, it may designate an enemy Character model. Until the end of the turn, friendly units targeting that Character gain Sniper.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Soul Trap" hidden="false" id="75c5-7c2a-7031-ff18" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Soul Trap" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="a7c7-abae-8862-a2b6">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">*An arcane containment system that binds fragments of defeated enemies into its bearer's combat essence.* If a model equipped with a soul trap destroys an enemy Character in Melee, it gains +1 Strength, +1 Toughness, and +1 Attack. If the destroyed model was the Warlord, the controlling player instead gains +2 Victory Points. These effects persist for the remainder of the battle.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Spirit Probe" hidden="false" id="a22c-e717-9f73-aa1a" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Spirit Probe" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="5fbf-813f-3970-3ab9">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">Friendly Drukhari units within 6" of one or more models with a spirit probe may re-roll To Hit rolls of 1.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Stinger Pods" hidden="false" id="cba7-3d91-0f1d-307d" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Stinger Pods" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="f0d7-8f10-1f2f-97b4">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">*Toxin dispersal systems that release airborne micro-toxin clouds as the bearer passes over enemy infantry.* When a model equipped with stinger pods moves over an enemy Infantry unit during any Movement phase, that unit suffers D3 Strength 1 AP - Hits with Poisoned (4+) and Pinning. If the model's Movement is 14 or higher, it suffers D6 Hits instead. These hits are resolved as shooting attacks.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Tormentors" hidden="false" id="fd96-c56f-dd44-a30f" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Tormentors" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="db94-1950-a65a-de2a">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">*Psycho-reactive fear generators and neural torment engines designed to assault the minds of nearby prey with waves of panic and hallucinatory agony.* A model equipped with tormentors gains Fear (1) and a 6+ Invulnerable Save.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <infoLinks>
        <infoLink name="Invulnerable Save (X)" id="cdca-7586-98c4-1f76" hidden="false" targetId="2d12-951d-7304-58f8" type="rule">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" field="name" value="Invulnerable Save (6+)" />
          </modifiers>
        </infoLink>
      </infoLinks>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Trophy Rack" hidden="false" id="9397-906a-0ba6-dd1e" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Trophy Rack" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="afca-ea38-a018-859d">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">*Psycho-resonant terror amplifiers built from preserved victim remains infused with neural echo fragments.* Enemy units within 6" of one or more models equipped with trophy racks must re-roll successful Morale tests, Pinning tests, and Fear tests.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Venom Sails" hidden="false" id="469c-444f-451c-b00d" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Venom Sails" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="0c1c-a157-8867-337e">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">*Aerodynamic displacement sails that convert motion into evasive vector distortion fields.* A model equipped with venom sails gains Fleet (2). If it already has Fleet, increase its value by +1 to a maximum of 4. In addition, after completing a Charge, the model gains Hit &amp; Run until the end of the turn.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Webway Rift Generator" hidden="false" id="abe4-b75f-486d-d7d8" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Webway Rift Generator" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="4e88-5da7-d97b-d752">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">*A dimensional stabilization system that creates controlled breaches into the Webway for the deployment and extraction of Drukhari forces.* A model equipped with a webway rift generator gains Deep Strike. In addition, friendly units arriving from Reserves within 6" of one or more such models may re-roll Reserve rolls and Scatter dice when deploying via Deep Strike.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="upgrade" import="true" name="Venom Skimmer" hidden="false" id="4004-cc20-4aea-d4a3" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <profiles>
        <profile name="Venom Skimmer" typeId="2a1f-7837-f0ef-be44" typeName="Wargear Item" hidden="false" id="de57-9697-0b07-4370">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Description" typeId="347e-ee4a-764f-6be3">*A compact anti-grav assault platform for rapid insertion raids, precision skirmishing and high-speed harassment warfare. Larger and more stable than Reaver jetbikes, Venom skimmers trade some manoeuvrability for weapons integration, passenger stabilization and battlefield endurance.* A model equipped with a Venom skimmer gains the Cavalry (Antigrav) unit type and has its Movement characteristic set to 14. The model treats all terrain as open ground for movement purposes unless explicitly prohibited by scenario rules or battlefield conditions. The model gains Hammer of Wrath (2), Fleet (1), and Hit &amp; Run. A Venom skimmer has a Transport Capacity of 6 models. Models with the Bulky (X) special rule count as additional models as normal. Models in Terminator Armour, Heavy units, Monstrous units, or models mounted on Cavalry (Antigrav) may not embark unless explicitly stated otherwise. A Venom skimmer is equipped with a twin-linked splinter rifle.</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry type="unit" import="true" name="Archon" hidden="false" id="786f-5326-4e60-88f8" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <infoLinks>
        <infoLink name="Xenos" id="a419-131a-9381-29f6" hidden="false" targetId="e6a0-8f13-d5c2-4b79" type="rule" />
        <infoLink name="Aeldari (X)" id="0814-ecc4-8335-2882" hidden="false" targetId="fbd1-9907-8259-c689" type="rule">
          <modifiers>
            <modifier type="set" field="name" value="Aeldari (Drukhari, Kabal)" />
