  <sharedRules>
    <rule name="Aeldari (X)" id="fbd1-9907-8259-c689" hidden="false" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <description>The unit's civilization keyword and, after it, its Drukhari faction (Kabal, Wych Cult, Haemonculus Coven, Incubi or Hired Blades). Aeldari (Drukhari) units may only be selected in armies whose Civilization keyword is Drukhari unless specifically stated otherwise, and may not be selected within the same Primary Detachment as Asuryani units. The full civilization rules are in the Aeldari document.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Drukhari Skimmers" id="1aa3-0e26-5971-64cf" hidden="false" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <description>Drukhari Antigrav vehicles may move over other models and terrain as long as they do not end on top of them†.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Night Vision" id="bb43-b436-18ab-1c61" hidden="false" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <description>A unit that contains at least one model with this Special Rule ignores the effects of Night Fighting (see page 308) and no model may make Shrouded rolls to negate Wounds or Hull Points inflicted by their attacks.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Stealth" id="bed8-2ae0-01e6-b91d" hidden="false" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <description>If the model has not moved this turn, it cannot be targeted by ranged attacks from more than 12" away.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Ancient Cruelty" id="35e8-efd2-8291-0b9f" hidden="false" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <description>*The ancient nobility of Commorragh are masters of calculated violence, striking with cold precision to eliminate leaders, sow terror and collapse resistance.* A model with this Special Rule gains Fear (1), Precision Shots (5+) and Precision Strikes (5+). In addition, attacks made by character models with this Special Rule against Characters gain Murderous Strike (6+).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Arena Killers" id="ed40-2e66-4edc-4a88" hidden="false" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <description>*These warriors are consummate gladiators, masters of spectacle, precision and humiliation in close combat.* A model with this Special Rule gains Fleet (1), Precision Shots (6+) and Precision Strikes (6+). In addition, while involved in a Challenge, a model with this Special Rule gains Reach (1), Fearless and Battle-hardened (2).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Blade Artists" id="344a-9fe3-2879-545c" hidden="false" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <description>Models with this Special Rule gain Rending (6+) and Sudden Strike (1). If a character model already possesses either of these Special Rules, improve their value by +1 instead, to a maximum of 4+ for Rending and 4 for Sudden Strike.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Combat Drugs (X)" id="c076-e675-7af7-9383" hidden="false" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <description>*The Drukhari make extensive use of psycho-reactive stimulants, adrenal catalysts and hyper-aggressive chemical compounds designed to heighten combat performance beyond natural limits.* A unit with Combat Drugs (X) must roll X D6 before deployment and apply the corresponding effects from the table below for the duration of the battle. Unless otherwise stated, duplicate results have no additional effect. If a result would grant a Special Rule the unit already possesses, increase the value of that Special Rule by +1 instead, to a maximum of 4 unless otherwise specified. D6: Combat Drug, Effect. 1: Hypex, The unit gains Fleet (2).. 2: Grave Lotus, The unit gains Furious Charge (1).. 3: Serpentin, The unit gains Sudden Strike (1).. 4: Painbringer, The unit gains Feel No Pain (6+). Feel No Pain granted by this rule may not be improved beyond Feel No Pain (4+).. 5: Adrenalight, The unit gains Rage (2). If the unit already has Rage, increase its value by +1 instead, to a maximum of 3.. 6: Splintermind, The unit gains Counter-Attack (1) and Fear (1). Fear granted by this rule does not scale..</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Fleshcrafted Horror" id="2d14-16d5-f06e-face" hidden="false" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <description>A model with this Special Rule gains It Will Not Die (6+). If it already has It Will Not Die, improve it by +1 instead, to a maximum of It Will Not Die (5+).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Kabalite Discipline" id="c898-4bc6-958e-09cb" hidden="false" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <description>*Kabalite Warriors prosecute raids with cold precision, coordinating overlapping fire and surgical elimination strikes against vulnerable prey.* A unit with this Special Rule gains Precision Shots (6+). In addition, when targeting Pinned, Falling Back or Disordered enemy units, ranged attacks made by this unit gain Breaching (6+).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Lightning Blows (X)" id="9904-3c53-7057-b254" hidden="false" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <description>*Some warriors fight with such speed and precision that they are capable of landing a series of blows like lightning, before their opponent can even react. There are few that can withstand such a barrage of attacks, and those warriors that have mastered this technique are rightfully feared on the battlefield.* After normal To Hit rolls for a weapon with this special rule have been made, count the number of Hits inflicted on a roll of equal to or more than the value listed in brackets as part of this rule. Immediately resolve a number of additional To Hit rolls on the same unit using the attacking models' WS equal to the number of Hits counted earlier – any Hits scored roll To Wound as normal using the profile of the weapon with this special rule or a weapon chosen from those available to the model with this special rule if the rule is not applied to a specific weapon. These additional attacks do not themselves benefit from the Lightning Blows (X) special rule, but do benefit from any other special rules possessed by the attacking model, such as Preferred Enemy (X) or Precision Strikes (X).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Master of the Arena" id="f9f5-cea7-76d4-3410" hidden="false" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <description>Wych Cult Troops units in an army that includes one or more Succubus models gain the Line Unit Sub-type.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Master of Blades" id="f4a4-03fd-3eee-9723" hidden="false" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <description>Incubi units in an army that includes one or more models with this special rule gain the Line Unit Sub-type.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Master of the Coven" id="e3fa-8751-c18c-36c9" hidden="false" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <description>Coven Troops units in an army that includes one or more Haemonculus models gain the Line Unit Sub-type.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Master Fleshcrafter" id="4f94-d17e-ba0d-9577" hidden="false" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <description>Friendly Wracks, Grotesques, Talos and Cronos units within 6" of one or more friendly models with this special rule gain +1 to Feel No Pain rolls, to a maximum of Feel No Pain (4+).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Master of the Kabal" id="5d9f-5b00-6524-9f3e" hidden="false" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <description>Kabalite Warriors Troops units in an army that includes one or more Archon models gain the Line Unit Sub-type.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Master of the Raid" id="661c-0af7-815d-43b3" hidden="false" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <description>Master of the Raid is the Drukhari equivalent of the Master of the Legion special rule and represents supreme battlefield authority within a Drukhari raiding force. Individuals possessing this rule are among the highest-ranking Archons, Succubi, or Haemonculi of Commorragh, commanding vast realspace raids through terror, manipulation, and overwhelming tactical brutality. A Detachment whose Primary HQ choice possesses the Master of the Raid special rule may select a Drukhari Rite of Raid. Unless otherwise specified, only one Rite of Raid may be chosen for each Primary Detachment. In addition, a Detachment led by a model with Master of the Raid may include a single Retinue unit that does not use up a Force Organization slot. Such a unit must begin the game joined to the model with this special rule unless explicitly stated otherwise. A model with Master of the Raid gains the Fear (1) special rule if it does not already possess it. Friendly Drukhari units within 12" of one or more models with this special rule may use the controlling player's choice of Leadership characteristic when taking Pinning tests, Regroup tests, or Morale checks caused by Shooting attacks. A Primary Detachment may only include a single model with the Master of the Raid special rule unless explicitly stated otherwise by a Rite of Raid.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Poison Masters" id="fffb-3669-7fd9-fd9a" hidden="false" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <description>Weapons used by a model with this Special Rule improve their Poisoned (X) value by +1 (Poisoned (4+) becomes Poisoned (3+)). A weapon without the Poisoned special rule instead gains Poisoned (6+).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Power From Pain" id="ceac-7e1a-2851-4684" hidden="false" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <description>*The Drukhari feed upon terror, suffering, and the collapse of both friend and foe alike, descending into ecstatic states of violence as battle intensifies.* At the start of each Phase, a unit with this Special Rule may select one effect, unless otherwise specified, from the table below whose listed condition is currently being met. Each unit selects its effect independently. Condition: Effect. Enemy unit within 12" Falling Back, Pinned, or Disordered: Fleet (1). Enemy unit within 12" has suffered one or more casualties this Phase: Fleet (1), Sudden Strike (1). Enemy unit within 12" is Below Half Strength: Fleet (2), Sudden Strike (2). A friendly Wych unit has been destroyed during the battle: Rampage (1). A friendly Wych Independent Character has been removed as a casualty during the battle: Rage (2). An enemy Character has been removed as a casualty during the battle: Furious Charge (1). The enemy Warlord has been removed as a casualty during the battle: Furious Charge (2). An enemy unit has been destroyed during the battle: Feel No Pain (6+). An enemy Lord of War has been destroyed during the battle: Battle-hardened (2), Rampage (2). An enemy Primarch has been removed as a casualty during the battle: Feel No Pain (4+), Furious Charge (2), Fleet (2), Rage (2).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Reservoir of Pain" id="d1f2-43d1-d6e6-2b23" hidden="false" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <description>Whenever a model equipped with spirit-leech tentacles inflicts one or more unsaved Wounds that result in an enemy model being removed as a casualty during the Assault phase, the controlling player may select either the attacking unit or a single friendly Drukhari Infantry unit within 6" of the attacking unit. After all attacks for that combat have been resolved, the selected unit immediately regains a single lost Wound previously suffered during the battle. If no model in the selected unit has lost any Wounds, but the unit has suffered casualties earlier in the battle, a single previously removed model may instead be returned to the unit with a remaining Wounds characteristic of 1. A model returned to play by Reservoir of Pain must be placed in unit coherency. If the unit is locked in combat, the returned model may be placed in base contact with an enemy model already engaged with that unit. Character models returned to play by Reservoir of Pain do not grant additional Victory Points if removed as casualties again later in the battle.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Shadowborn" id="3797-a365-c776-96b2" hidden="false" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <description>*These creatures drift through darkness like living nightmares, emerging from impossible angles amidst shadow and fear before vanishing once more into the gloom.* A unit with this Special Rule gains Infiltrate, Shrouded and Fear (1). In addition, enemy units treat models with this Special Rule as being 6" further away when making ranged attacks against them. Finally, enemy units arriving via Deep Strike within 3" of one or more models with this Special Rule suffer a Disordered Deep Strike Assault on a roll of 1, 2, or 3. Enemy units arriving via Deep Strike within 6" of one or more models with this Special Rule suffer a Disordered Deep Strike Assault on a roll of 1 or 2.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Terror Tactics" id="acb9-121b-7a20-0918" hidden="false" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <description>A model with this Special Rule gains Fear (1). If it already has Fear, increase its value by +1 instead, to a maximum of Fear (3).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Webway Assault" id="e243-ef7e-4142-3865" hidden="false" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <description>*The Drukhari strike from hidden dimensional corridors and concealed webway breaches, descending upon their prey with terrifying speed and precision before vanishing once more into the void between worlds.* If a unit with this Special Rule arrives from Reserves during the current Turn, it gains Fleet (2), Sudden Strike (2) and Shrouded (6+). If a unit with this Special Rule already possesses Fleet or Sudden Strike, increase their value by +1 instead, to a maximum of 4. If a unit already possesses Shrouded, improve its value by +1 instead, to a maximum of Shrouded (4+). A unit may only benefit from Webway Assault during the Turn in which it arrived from Reserves unless otherwise specified.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Bio-Construct" id="a56e-a0ab-6807-b952" hidden="false" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <description>*The Bio-Construct Unit Type represents grotesque fleshcrafted war-engines, pain engines, and surgically augmented monstrosities created by the Haemonculus Covens. Though biologically derived, these entities function on the battlefield in a manner comparable to Dreadnoughts, combining unnatural durability, integrated heavy weapon systems, and catastrophic close combat lethality within massively reinforced fleshcraft bodies. Bio-Constructs are sustained through layered biological redundancy, pain suppression matrices, vat-grown organ reinforcement, and psycho-reactive regenerative systems. Their bodies are resistant to conventional toxins and biological attack vectors, while invasive neural conditioning renders them incapable of fear or hesitation. Many Bio-Constructs also contain volatile animus-reactors, pain engines, or soul-furnaces that detonate violently upon catastrophic destruction.* Any rule, effect, weapon, or special rule that specifically affects models of the Dreadnought Unit Type also affects models with the Bio-Construct Unit Type unless explicitly stated otherwise. The following rules apply to all models with the Bio-Construct Unit Type and any Bio-Construct sub-types: Successful Wounds scored by attacks with the Poisoned or Fleshbane special rules must be re-rolled against models of the Bio-Construct Unit Type. All Bio-Construct models have the Fearless special rule. A model with the Bio-Construct Unit Type may fire all weapons they are equipped with in each Shooting Attack they make, including as part of a Reaction. A model of the Bio-Construct Unit Type may fire Heavy and Ordnance weapons and counts as Stationary even if it moved in the preceding Movement phase, and may declare Charges as normal regardless of any Shooting Attacks made in the same turn. No model that is not also of the Bio-Construct Unit Type may join a unit that includes a Bio-Construct model. Any model with the Bio-Construct Unit Type that suffers an unsaved Wound with the Instant Death special rule is not immediately removed as a casualty, but instead loses D3 Wounds instead of one for each unsaved Wound with the Instant Death special rule inflicted upon it. In addition, when a model with the Bio-Construct Unit Type loses its last Wound, but before it is removed as a casualty, all models, friendly and enemy, within D6" suffer an automatic Hit at Strength 8, AP -.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Soul-leech" id="e4a1-2ed2-3b1c-730f" hidden="false" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <description>Each time the bearer inflicts an unsaved Wound with the Parasite's Kiss, it immediately gains back one Wound it lost previously in the battle.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Entangle" id="1687-2ce3-fccd-0366" hidden="false" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <description>Models affected by a shardnet and impaler suffer -2 Initiative (to a minimum of 1) until the end of the Fight phase. In addition, they may not make Reactions that involve movement disengagement unless they pass a Leadership test.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Sub-faction (X)" id="6c34-8d21-1695-b14f" hidden="false" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <description>Every Drukhari detachment fights for one of the three great powers of Commorragh: the Kabals, the Wych Cults or the Haemonculus Covens. Choose one when building each detachment, then one of its Obsessions (below). The sub-faction gives that detachment its Advanced Reaction, Warlord Trait and Line units.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Obsession (X)" id="3bf4-f7e6-59c2-d363" hidden="false" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <description>When building an army, choose one Obsession of the detachment's sub-faction for each detachment. Every unit in that detachment gains Obsession (X), where X is the chosen Obsession. Unique characters may join any Obsession of their sub-faction, except Lelith Hesperax (Cult of Strife), Asdrubael Vect (Kabal of the Black Heart) and Urien Rakarth (Prophets of Flesh).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule name="Invulnerable Save (X)" id="2d12-951d-7304-58f8" hidden="false" publicationId="9356-fc9b-2fee-7d11">
      <description>The model has an Invulnerable Save of X, which may be taken against any Wound instead of its armour save.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
